#!/bin/bash
# -*- sh -*-

: << =cut

=head1 NAME

amd_gpu_ - Wildcard plugin to monitor AMD GPUs. Uses rocm-smi utility
(ROCm System Management Interface) to obtain information.

=head1 CONFIGURATION

This is a wildcard plugin. The wildcard prefix link name should be the
value to monitor.

This plugin uses the following configuration variables:

 [amd_gpu_*]
  env.warning - Warning temperature
  env.critical - Critical temperature

=head2 DEFAULT CONFIGURATION

The default configuration is to set warning and critical temperatures of
75 and 95 degrees celsius, respectively.

=head2 EXAMPLE WILDCARD USAGE

C<ln -s /usr/share/munin/plugins/amd_gpu_ /etc/munin/plugins/amd_gpu_temp>

...will monitor the temperature of available GPUs.

=head1 NOTES

- Requires rocm-smi with --json support and jq installed.
- ROCm 4.0+ uses separate flags (e.g. --showmetrics, --showmemuse) instead
  of the -q query flag. This plugin calls rocm-smi -a --json for a complete
  JSON snapshot. Older ROCm versions that lack -a --json will not work.
- On some AMD consumer cards (RX series), PCIe cumulative bandwidth counters
  (rx/tx) report "N/A". This is a hardware/driver limitation, not a plugin
  issue.
- Fan speed may report "0" on passively-cooled cards or when idle.

=head1 TODO

=over 4

=item *

Add support for per-GPU VRAM absolute values (used/free in MiB).

=back

=head1 AUTHOR

Based on nvidia_gpu_ by Nuno Fachada (faken@fakenmc.com)

